SOUTH-CORE

An ongoing engineering investigation into building resilient, offline-first systems for real-world environments.

Current Phase

Problem Investigation

SOUTH-CORE begins with a simple principle:

«Understand the problem before designing the solution.»

We are investigating real-world environments, identifying where important information or capabilities become unavailable, measuring the consequences, challenging assumptions, and documenting what we learn.

No final solution has been chosen yet.

Engineering Process

Understand
    ↓
Build
    ↓
Break
    ↓
Fix
    ↓
Prove
    ↓
Commit

The project history is part of the project.

Investigations, failed assumptions, design changes, experiments, measurements, failures, fixes, and decisions will be documented rather than hidden.

